[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   Step 127 -- Non-Warsaw two-leg refit: carrier-degeneracy close.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   The transit channel (steps 030-086) rests on the three-leg catalogue
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   record: separate orbit solutions fitted to pre- and post-perihelion
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   astrometry, all of Warsaw-school lineage (CODE / Warsaw / CometEls).
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   The registered vulnerability (T9 audit, step_123) is that a shared
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   fitting pipeline could manufacture the observable; step_124 showed
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   the spatial aphelion channel survives on reconstruction-free SBDB
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   elements, but the rotation/slip channel had never been replicated by
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   an independent fitter.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   This step builds that independent fitter.  For every pre-2018 LPC
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   cohort member (step_b84) in the MPC-astrometry era (perihelion year
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   >= 1950) it
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   1. pulls the raw MPC observation record for the comet
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   (data.minorplanetcenter.net get-obs, ADES_DF), cached under
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   data/raw/mpc/obs/;
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   2. pulls the full-precision SBDB solution purely as an orbit seed
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   (data/raw/mpc/sbdb_fp/), cached;
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   3. splits the observations at perihelion and fits each leg
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   independently by Levenberg-Marquardt differential correction on
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   the Cartesian state at the leg mid-epoch (6 parameters,
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   REBOUND/IAS15 + DE440s force model identical to the boundary
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   integrator, one-way light-time correction, topocentric
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   parallax from the MPC observatory table, MAD outlier clip);
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   4. propagates each fitted leg to the +/-250 AU barycentric sphere
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   with the same integrate_leg machinery the catalogue record
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   uses, yielding a zero-Warsaw-lineage boundary record per comet:
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   our drot (full-arc fit propagated both ways), our ddirf
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   (independent-leg orig-vs-future analogue), our energy kick daa
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   and encounter distance denc, our aphelion axis angle theta.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   Registered tests
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   T1  fitter validity: per-comet Spearman concordance of our drot vs
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   the catalogue drot on the shared cohort, plus element-level
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   agreement of our full-arc fit against its SBDB seed.  If the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   instrument works, both must concord.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   T2  rotation-per-encounter-kick residual cap contrast on the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   independent record: log10(drot) regressed on
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   log10(|daa|+1), log10(denc), q, i exactly as in steps
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   117/120/123; Mann-Whitney in-cap vs out at 60 deg on OUR theta,
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   with a label-shuffle permutation null, reported beside the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   catalogue-side contrast recomputed on the identical members.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   This symmetric channel is flat on BOTH records -- the catalogue
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   itself registers no raw drot cap contrast on the fittable
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   subset.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   T2b DECISIVE -- the registered carrier channel (step_123): the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   inbound-leg deviation d_in = sep(inbound boundary asymptote,
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   osculating periapsis direction).  The step_123 audit localized
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   the catalogue anomaly to this channel (in-cap excess p = 0.042
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   with the outbound leg flat).  T2b tests whether the SAME in-cap
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   excess survives on the zero-Warsaw-lineage fits, on identical
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   members, against the catalogue-side contrast recomputed on the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   same set.  Replication here closes the lineage objection: the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   anomaly lives in the astrometry, not in the Warsaw pipeline.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   T3  independent-leg disagreement: cap contrast of our ddirf and
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   its concordance with the catalogue rotation -- the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   orig-vs-future analogue built from fits that never shared an
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   orbit solution.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   T4  cross-arc prediction: our inbound fit propagated FORWARD to
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   the withheld outbound observations -- rms misfit, in-cap vs
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   out.  A pure-gravity single-orbit world predicts equal
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   extrapolation loss both ways; the NG-floor controls are the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   same for all comets so a cap-asymmetric extrapolation penalty
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   is a candidate physical discriminator.
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   T5  audit: fit quality (rms per leg), cohort yield, and the
[2026-10-16 13:44:38 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 127]   per-leg observation floor.
